  "title": "Town Clerk – Town of Hancock",
  "text": "Town Clerk – Town of Hancock\nTown of Hancock\nDepartments\nCalendar\nForms\nContact\nPoints of Interest\nAttractions / Misc.\nCamping\nFood\nLodging\nPhotos\nPayments\nTown Clerk\nLinda Burdick, Town Clerk\nHours at the Town Hall – Thursdays from 8:00 – noon\n1st Saturday of every month – 9:00 – 11:00 a.m.\nMailing Address:\nPO Box 1097\nHancock, MA 01237\nEmail:\nclerk@town.hancock.ma.us\nPhone number:\n(413) 738-5225 Option# 2\nPayments can be made online:\nhttps://unipaygold.unibank.com/CustomerInfo.aspx?Customerid=2366\nWE CANNOT ACCEPT CASH.  Please make out checks or money orders to the Town of Hancock.\nForms and Documents:\nBusiness Certificate Application\nDog License Request Renewal Form-1\n2025 Annual Election Results(1)\nEthics Training and Open Meeting Law\nNotice to Dog Owners\nPublic Records Access\nRequest For Vital Record\nTown Clerk Fee Schedule\nUnderground/Above Ground Certification-1\nVoter Registration and Absentee Ballot\nHancock is a quiet, peaceful town about twenty miles long and three miles wide, bordered on the east by the famous Berkshire hills, and on the west by the rugged Taconic range.\nHancock is the longest and narrowest town in Berkshire County.  The northern portion of the town is separated from the southern portion by a mountain.  One has to drive through a couple of towns to the east or drive west into New York to get from one end to the other.\n413-738-5225\n3650 Hancock Road\nPO Box 1084, Hancock, MA 01237\nThe Town Hall is open every week day (except holidays) between 9:00 AM and 12:00 noon.",
